      "message": "This is speculative, but you could get a CC connected event between the CC read and re-arming the interrupt, and that event might be lost. Re-arming first and then reading would avoid that race.\n\n```suggestion\n        it8xxx2_tcpm_enable_plug_in_detect(port);\n\n        it8xxx2_tcpm_get_cc(port, \u0026cc1, \u0026cc2);\n        if (!cc_is_open(cc1, cc2) \u0026\u0026 !cc_is_pwred_cbl_without_snk(cc1, cc2))\n            task_set_event(PD_PORT_TO_TASK_ID(port), PD_EVENT_CC);\n```",
